amux direct — direct client access (web, Android) over your LAN or VPN (opt-in, host only)

usage: amux direct <command>

The direct server is an opt-in HTTPS listener on a private address. Clients
enroll with a one-time code you paste or scan (enroll --qr), then reach this
host's sessions with destination-issued credentials. No cloud service is in
the path. See docs/direct-access.md.

Disabling the managed listener is not revocation: clients stay enrolled and
the cloud policy stays as it is. Use amux direct clients revoke and amux
direct cloud disable for those.

commands:
  enable [flags]        save the listener settings and turn it on (the daemon runs it from now on)
  disable [--no-wait]   turn the managed listener off (settings, clients and cloud policy are kept)
  status [--json]       setting, managed listener, server and provider offer
  logs [-n lines]       the managed listener's log
  serve [flags]         run the direct server in the foreground (manual)
  enroll [flags]        mint a one-time enrollment code: a bundle to paste, or a QR code to scan
  clients <command>     list, update or revoke enrolled clients
  audit [--client <id>] [--limit N] [--json]
                        answers, item triage and overseer steers made by direct clients (newest last)
  reset-identity --yes  replace the server identity; revokes every client and disables cloud enrollment
  cloud <command>       cloud-assisted enrollment policy (off by default)
  wake <command>        content-free cloud wake-ups for direct clients (opt-in)

Run 'amux direct <command> --help' for details.
